── UNKNOWN NAME ────────────────────────────── E0211_error_type.lt:1:27  [E0211]

Stilt has no `error` type: a function that can fail raises its own error type:

  1 │ fn parse(s: str) -> (i64, error) {
    │                           ^^^^^

A function's row names the type of what it raises, as `/ raise<ParseError>`, and
`try f() catch e => …` handles it.
